body:
@DaveCTurner To clarify ... from the point of view of a management UX, if a snapshot repo is unhealthy, I'd expect to see a human-readable (and hopefully actionable) error, likely in the `Repositories` tab. I would expect to be able to list the snapshots that were available to me (with UI indicators if some repos were unavailable). I would never expect a user to have to exclude/pick/interact with a list of repos in order to list snapshots. But I would expect they could use filters, such as repo name, if they had a long list of snapshots.

If using the snapshots API with some sort of automation tooling, then maybe strict failures is more appropriate. However for a human clicking around a UI, for this particular use case, leniency would be preferred.

Thx for improving the error.
